A||N||4||Haze_Performance||Big Time Computer Problems (PLEASE HELP)||||9||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-01-2000||05:12 AM||||I have a New Laptop with Win98 (Digital Hi Note Ultra 2000). I just picked up a printer. (Lexmark Z52) I installed it and all looks fine. BUT......when I try to print it will take in the paper ok....but it wont print..after about 3sec it goes Offline & the paper stays in untill I turn it off(Thats what the status bar says)Whats worng?? The Printer looks fine. No paper jam...No flashing lights...Nothing. (Im using the Parallel port)<P><BR>Problem #2<P>I just got Print Shop Deluxe. When I install the CD it wont load. I tried to run (D:\SETUP.EXE) still nothing. That says it cant find the path. But all mt other programs will auto run when I drop the CD's in.<P>HELP!!!!!!!!!!!!I need my Printer to Work + Print Shop!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||fierospeeder||08-01-2000||06:28 AM||||is it those portable printers?  that you have to have the printer verticle so the paper can go through?   <P>If your printer is setup correctly, when you click print, you should hear the printer move after.<BR>Also, look in your manual, there are test buttons that will print up different characters on paper without having the computer on.<P>With the CD, try putting it in your other computer and see if it works.  Try a normal CD also, during this time.  If another CD works at the present time and not yesterday then your cd is bad.  Unless you tried a CD 2 hours ago, and your cd drivers got removed and you tried this new cd and it doesn't read.  Means you have to reinstall your drivers.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-01-2000||09:12 AM||||#1... What are you trying to print?<BR>Maybe try something from a different app.<BR>Also, If your Lexmark disk is like ours, all the drivers for all the printers are on the CD. Be sure you've got the right driver.<BR>If it gives you an option, try loading the PCL driver for your printer, instead of the PS driver. (More "generic".)<P>#2... Go to Windows Explorer (or My Computer). Navigate to the "D" drive. Look in the root directory of the CD. You should be able to see the "exe" file. It's usually "setup.exe", but it might be "install.exe", or some such.<BR>  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||08-02-2000||02:58 AM||||go to a dos prompt and type "echo test&gt;lpt1" and see if anything comes out of the printer. if it does print the word test, then you know it is the software. email me, i get to fix these things for a living||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||08-03-2000||11:26 AM||||Thanks for the help guys.. I went and got a new printer and its doing the same thing. Im going to bring the computer to CompUSA to get it repaired.<P><BR>Thanks Again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||14
